    "description": "Build a streaming data processing pipeline using Apache Flink or Spark Streaming to preprocess and enrich real-time transportation data. This includes filtering, aggregation, feature extraction, and data enrichment with historical context.",
    "implementationGuide": "1. Implement data preprocessing operators (filtering, normalization, deduplication)\n2. Create feature extraction functions (traffic density, congestion patterns, travel time estimates)\n3. Implement data enrichment with historical data and contextual information\n4. Set up state management for real-time aggregations\n5. Implement windowing operations for time-based analysis\n6. Create data quality checks and anomaly detection",
    "notes": "Focus on low-latency processing, handle data skew, implement checkpointing for fault tolerance.",
    "dependencies": ["Real-time Data Ingestion System"],
    "relatedFiles": [
      {
        "path": "code/processing_pipeline.py",
        "type": "CREATE",
        "description": "Streaming data processing pipeline with Flink/Spark Streaming"
      },
      {
        "path": "code/feature_extraction.py",
        "type": "CREATE",
        "description": "Feature extraction and data enrichment functions"
      }
    ],
    "verificationCriteria": "Processing pipeline handles 10,000+ events/second with <500ms end-to-end latency. Feature extraction produces accurate and consistent results. Data quality checks catch 99% of anomalies. System is fault-tolerant with proper checkpointing."
  },
  {
    "name": "AI/ML Model Development for Route Optimization",
    "description": "Develop and train AI/ML models for route optimization using deep learning techniques. This includes building Graph Neural Networks (GNN) or Reinforcement Learning models that can predict optimal routes based on real-time traffic conditions and historical patterns.",
    "implementationGuide": "1. Collect and preprocess historical transportation data for training\n2. Design and implement Graph Neural Network architecture for route representation\n3. Implement Reinforcement Learning environment for route optimization\n4. Train models using TensorFlow/PyTorch with appropriate loss functions\n5. Implement model evaluation and validation framework\n6. Create model serving infrastructure with TensorFlow Serving or TorchServe",
    "notes": "Use transfer learning from existing models, implement model versioning, ensure model interpretability.",
    "dependencies": ["Real-time Data Processing Pipeline"],
    "relatedFiles": [
      {
        "path": "code/models/route_optimizer.py",
        "type": "CREATE",
        "description": "Main route optimization model implementation"
      },
